window.AG_PRACTICE["anquan"] = {"id":"anquan","axis":"needle","seal":"安","scene":"art/scene-treatment.jpg","title":"Needling Safety","titleZh":"針刺安全","sub":"Forbidden points, pregnancy points, angle and depth, and the accidents","subZh":"禁針穴、孕婦禁穴、針刺角度深淺，與針刺意外","mentor":{"key":"shen","nm":"Master Shen","nmZh":"參師父","line":"\"There is no such thing as a dangerous point. There is a wrong angle and a wrong depth, and the point is where you find out.\"","lineZh":"「無所謂危險之穴。有誤之角度、誤之深淺，而穴者，其見分曉之處耳。」"},"card":{"h":"Angle and Depth Are the Answer","hZh":"所答者，角度與深淺","p":"On the acupuncture paper, a safety question is almost never asking whether a point is allowed. It is asking for the angle, the depth, or the direction you must not go. Zhongfu is needled obliquely and laterally, never deeply toward the midline. Tiantu goes in perpendicular for a fifth of an inch and then turns downward behind the manubrium. Juque may be needled downward but never deeply upward. Shenque is not needled at all. Learn each one as a sentence with a direction in it, and the answer comes out whole.","pZh":"針灸卷上之安全題，所問者鮮少為「此穴可否針」，而為其角度、深淺，或其所不可向。中府向外斜刺，不可向內深刺；天突先直刺二分，而後轉向下沿胸骨柄後緣；巨闕可向下而不可向上深刺；神闕則根本不針。每穴記為一句含「方向」之語，其答自全。"},"items":[{"k":"mc","q":"Which is the correct needling of Zhongfu LU1, and what is the risk if you get it wrong?","qZh":"中府 LU1 之正確針法為何？誤之何險？","opts":[{"t":"Oblique insertion directed laterally, 0.5–0.8 cun — never deeply toward the midline, because of pneumothorax","c":"向外斜刺 0.5–0.8 寸；嚴禁向內深刺，恐致氣胸","ok":1,"note":"The direction is the answer. LU1 中府 sits in the 1st intercostal space, 6 cun lateral to the midline, with lung directly beneath — so the needle is angled <b>away</b> from the chest, never toward it. Your notes quote the <i>Su Wen</i> on this: needling into the depression of the chest and striking the lung causes wheezing and laboured breathing with the head held back. LU2 雲門 carries the same caution. 所答者其向也。中府在第一肋間隙，去前正中線六寸，其下即肺，故針當<b>向外</b>而不可向內。《素問·刺禁論》：刺膺中陷中肺，為喘逆仰息。雲門同此戒。"},{"t":"Perpendicular insertion 1.5 cun for a strong deqi","c":"直刺一寸半以求強得氣","ok":0,"note":"Depth is the danger. Perpendicular insertion at LU1 is limited to 0.3–0.5 cun in your notes, and 1.5 cun toward the chest is how a pneumothorax happens. 危在其深。課件所載中府直刺止於 0.3–0.5 寸；向胸深入一寸半，氣胸所由生也。"},{"t":"Transverse insertion toward the sternum","c":"向胸骨平刺","ok":0,"note":"Toward the midline is the forbidden direction, at any angle. 向內者，無論何角度，皆其所禁。"},{"t":"It is a forbidden point","c":"此為禁針穴","ok":0,"note":"It is not forbidden — it is the Front-Mu point of the Lung and used constantly. It is <i>angle-dependent</i>, which is a different thing and the thing the examination tests. 非禁針。中府為肺之募穴，用之甚常。其所係在角度，與「禁針」異，而考題所試者正在此。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which point on the Conception Vessel is absolutely forbidden to needle, and what is used instead?","qZh":"任脈何穴絕對禁針？當以何法代之？","opts":[{"t":"Shenque CV8, at the centre of the umbilicus — moxibustion only, on salt or on ginger","c":"神闕 CV8，臍中——只灸不針，隔鹽或隔薑","ok":1,"note":"Needling is strictly forbidden at CV8 神闕: the depth is written as 0.0 cun. Moxa on salt is the classical method and it is a first-choice treatment for stroke desertion patterns, coma, and deficiency-cold diarrhoea — so the point is important precisely <i>because</i> of the moxa, not despite the prohibition. 神闕嚴禁針刺，其深書為 0.0 寸。隔鹽灸為古法，主中風脫證、昏迷、虛寒泄瀉，皆第一要法。故此穴之要，正在其灸，非以其禁而輕之。"},{"t":"Guanyuan CV4","c":"關元 CV4","ok":0,"note":"CV4 關元 is needled perpendicularly 0.8–1.2 cun and is one of the great tonifying points. It carries a pregnancy caution and requires the bladder to be emptied first — cautions, not a prohibition. 關元直刺 0.8–1.2 寸，為大補元氣之要穴。其戒在孕，及刺前須排空膀胱——戒也，非禁也。"},{"t":"Zhongwan CV12","c":"中脘 CV12","ok":0,"note":"CV12 中脘 is needled 0.5–1.2 cun and is the Front-Mu of the Stomach and the Influential point of the Fu. 中脘直刺 0.5–1.2 寸，胃之募穴、腑會也。"},{"t":"Tiantu CV22","c":"天突 CV22","ok":0,"note":"CV22 天突 is needled, but by a two-stage technique — that is the next question. 天突可針，惟其法分二段，即下一題所問。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Describe the needling of Tiantu CV22.","qZh":"天突 CV22 之針法為何？","opts":[{"t":"Perpendicular 0.2–0.3 cun first; once past the inner border of the manubrium, turn the tip downward and insert slowly 0.5–1 cun along its posterior border, in front of the trachea. Do not retain.","c":"先直刺 0.2–0.3 寸；針尖過胸骨柄內緣後，轉向下沿其後緣緩進 0.5–1 寸，在氣管之前。不留針。","ok":1,"note":"A two-stage technique, and the turn is the whole point. Deep or continued perpendicular insertion risks <b>pneumothorax</b> and injury to the <b>trachea and great vessels</b>. Deqi is local soreness and distension with a tight, blocked feeling in the throat that disappears the moment the needle is withdrawn. 針分二段，其要在「轉」。若直刺過深或不轉，則有<b>氣胸</b>及傷<b>氣管、大血管</b>之虞。其得氣為局部痠脹，兼咽喉緊塞感，起針即失。"},{"t":"Perpendicular 1 cun in a single movement","c":"一次直刺一寸","ok":0,"note":"This is the error the two-stage technique exists to prevent. Straight down from the suprasternal fossa reaches the trachea and the great vessels. 二段之法，正為防此。自胸骨上窩直下，及氣管與大血管。"},{"t":"Oblique insertion upward toward the chin","c":"向頦部斜刺向上","ok":0,"note":"The direction is downward, behind the manubrium. Upward reaches nothing useful and risks the larynx. 其向在下，沿胸骨柄之後。向上則無所取，且有傷喉之虞。"},{"t":"Transverse insertion with the needle retained thirty minutes","c":"平刺並留針三十分鐘","ok":0,"note":"The needle is <i>not</i> retained at CV22. 天突不留針。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each Conception Vessel point to the caution your notes attach to it.","qZh":"任脈各穴，配其課件所載之戒。","pairs":[{"l":"CV8 Shenque 神闕","lZh":"神闕","r":"Needling strictly forbidden — moxa only","rZh":"嚴禁針刺，只灸"},{"l":"CV22 Tiantu 天突","lZh":"天突","r":"Two-stage insertion; do not needle deeply or perpendicularly","rZh":"分二段進針；不可直刺過深"},{"l":"CV23 Lianquan 廉泉","lZh":"廉泉","r":"Do not retain — swallowing can break the needle","rZh":"不可久留針，吞嚥可致斷針"},{"l":"CV14 Juque 巨闕","lZh":"巨闕","r":"Downward or perpendicular only — never deeply upward","rZh":"可直刺或向下斜刺，嚴禁向上深刺"},{"l":"CV3 Zhongji / CV4 Guanyuan 中極、關元","lZh":"中極、關元","r":"Empty the bladder before needling","rZh":"刺前須排空膀胱"}],"note":"Five points, five different reasons — a forbidden point, an angle, a retention rule, a direction, and a preparation. Safety questions on this channel almost always come from this list. 五穴五因：一禁針、一角度、一留針、一方向、一準備。本經之安全題，多出於此。"},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient is 11 weeks pregnant. Which Conception Vessel points do your notes mark with a pregnancy caution?","qZh":"妊娠十一週。課件於任脈何穴標「孕」？","opts":[{"t":"Most of the abdominal points — CV1 through CV7 and CV9 through CV13, plus CV24","c":"腹部諸穴幾皆有之——CV1–CV7、CV9–CV13，另有 CV24 承漿","ok":1,"note":"The Conception Vessel arises in the uterus and runs the midline of the abdomen, so nearly the whole abdominal run carries a pregnancy caution — CV1 會陰, CV2 曲骨, CV3 中極, CV4 關元 and CV5 石門 are marked forbidden as well as pregnancy-cautioned. Learn the shape rather than the list: on this channel, from the perineum to the epigastrium, assume caution and check. 任脈起於胞宮，循腹正中而上，故腹部一路幾皆有孕戒；會陰、曲骨、中極、關元、石門更兼「禁針」之標。宜記其形而不記其單：本經自會陰至上脘，先假定當慎，而後查之。"},{"t":"Only CV1 Huiyin","c":"惟會陰一穴","ok":0,"note":"Far too narrow. The caution runs the length of the abdomen. 太狹。其戒遍於腹部。"},{"t":"None — the Conception Vessel is the fertility channel","c":"皆無——任脈本主生育","ok":0,"note":"It governs fertility and the uterus, which is exactly why it is needled with caution in pregnancy. Function and safety are different questions. 其主胞胎，正以此故，妊娠用之尤當謹。功用與安全，二問也。"},{"t":"Only the chest points CV17 to CV22","c":"惟胸部 CV17–CV22","ok":0,"note":"Those carry angle and depth cautions, not pregnancy ones. 彼所戒在角度深淺，非在孕。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Your notes mark LU3 Tianfu with a caution that is not about needling. What is it?","qZh":"課件於天府 LU3 所標之戒，不在針而在何？","opts":[{"t":"Moxibustion is contraindicated 禁灸","ok":1,"note":"From the <i>Great Compendium</i>: moxibustion is contraindicated at LU3 天府; needle 0.4 cun, retain seven respirations. Worth noticing because most cautions you meet are about the needle — a point can be fine to needle and wrong to moxa, and the examination knows it. 《針灸大成》：天府禁灸，針四分，留七呼。當留意者：所遇之戒多在針，而一穴或可針而不可灸。此考試所知也。"},{"t":"It is forbidden in pregnancy 孕婦禁用","ok":0,"note":"That caution belongs to the abdominal points of the Conception Vessel, not to the upper arm. 此戒在任脈腹部諸穴，不在上臂。"},{"t":"There is an artery beneath it 其下有動脈","ok":0,"note":"The artery cautions on this channel are LU8 經渠 and LU9 太淵, both at the wrist beside the radial artery. 本經動脈之戒在經渠與太淵，皆在腕側橈動脈旁。"},{"t":"It may only be pricked to bleed 惟可點刺出血","ok":0,"note":"That is LU11 少商 — shallow insertion 0.1 cun, or prick to bleed. 此少商之法：淺刺一分，或點刺出血。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which Lung channel points carry an artery caution, and what does that change?","qZh":"肺經何穴有動脈之戒？其戒改何事？","opts":[{"t":"LU8 Jingqu and LU9 Taiyuan — both sit beside the radial artery, so insertion stays shallow and to the side of it","c":"經渠、太淵——二穴皆傍橈動脈，故宜淺刺而避之","ok":1,"note":"LU9 太淵 is at the radial end of the wrist crease, <b>radial to the radial artery</b>: perpendicular 0.3–0.5 cun, or 0.2–0.3 cun in your course notes, avoiding the vessel. LU8 經渠 sits in the depression between the radial styloid and the artery, 0.1–0.3 cun. The caution changes the depth and the exact spot, not whether you use them — LU9 is the Source point and the Influential point of the vessels. 太淵在腕橫紋橈側，<b>橈動脈之橈側</b>：直刺 0.3–0.5 寸，課件作 0.2–0.3 寸，避其脈。經渠在橈骨莖突與動脈之間凹陷，刺 0.1–0.3 寸。其戒所改者深淺與確切之位，非可否——太淵者，肺之原穴、八會之脈會也。"},{"t":"LU1 and LU2 — the subclavian artery","c":"中府、雲門——鎖骨下動脈","ok":0,"note":"Their caution is pneumothorax, and it is about direction. 彼所戒為氣胸，其事在向。"},{"t":"LU5 and LU6 — the brachial artery","c":"尺澤、孔最——肱動脈","ok":0,"note":"LU5 尺澤 is needled 0.5–1.2 cun or pricked to bleed; LU6 孔最 0.5–1.2 cun. Neither carries the artery mark in your notes. 尺澤刺 0.5–1.2 寸或點刺出血，孔最 0.5–1.2 寸。課件於二穴皆無動脈之標。"},{"t":"LU10 and LU11 — the digital arteries","c":"魚際、少商——指動脈","ok":0,"note":"LU10 is 0.5–1 cun; LU11 is shallow or pricked to bleed. Not marked. 魚際刺 0.5–1 寸；少商淺刺或點刺。皆無此標。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A first-time patient goes pale and sweaty and says she feels faint while the needles are in. What is the first move?","qZh":"初診病人留針之際，面色蒼白汗出，自言欲暈。首要處置為何？","opts":[{"t":"Withdraw the needles, lie her flat, raise the legs, keep her warm, and stay with her","c":"起針、令平臥、抬其足、保暖、守其側","ok":1,"note":"Needles out first — you cannot manage a fainting patient who is still pinned. Then flat with the legs raised so blood returns to the head. Note what produced it, because every one of these is preventable: a first treatment, an anxious or depleted patient, an empty stomach, sitting or standing rather than lying, and strong stimulation. That is why a first treatment is given lying down. 先起針——針猶在身，無以救其暈。次令平臥抬足，使血歸於上。當察其所由，蓋皆可防：初診、其人怯或虛、空腹、坐立受針、手法過重。故初診宜臥而受之。"},{"t":"Needle Renzhong DU26 before anything else","c":"先針人中 DU26","ok":0,"note":"DU26 is the revival point every textbook names, and it is not the <i>first</i> move. Position comes before points: needles out, flat, legs up. 人中誠為回蘇之穴，然非所先。體位在取穴之前：起針、平臥、抬足。"},{"t":"Sit her up slowly and give her water","c":"令緩緩坐起，予以飲水","ok":0,"note":"The wrong direction — sitting takes blood away from the head, which is what is already short. 其向適反：坐則血益去於上，而上本不足。"},{"t":"Leave the room to fetch your supervisor","c":"離室去請指導老師","ok":0,"note":"Call for help without leaving. A fainting patient with needles in is never left alone. 當呼人而不當離。留針而暈者，不可獨處。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each needling accident to its first response.","qZh":"針刺意外，各配其首要處置。","pairs":[{"l":"Fainting 暈針","lZh":"暈針","r":"Needles out, lie flat, legs up, keep warm","rZh":"起針、平臥、抬足、保暖"},{"l":"Stuck needle 滯針","lZh":"滯針","r":"Stop, let the muscle relax, massage around it — never force","rZh":"停手、令肌鬆、按其周圍——不可強拔"},{"l":"Bent needle 彎針","lZh":"彎針","r":"Do not rotate; withdraw slowly along the bend","rZh":"勿捻轉；順其彎徐徐退出"},{"l":"Broken needle 斷針","lZh":"斷針","r":"Keep the patient still, do not let them move, refer for removal","rZh":"令其勿動，速求取出"},{"l":"Haematoma 血腫","lZh":"血腫","r":"Press, cold first, then warmth and gentle massage later","rZh":"按壓、先冷敷，後乃溫敷輕揉"}],"note":"One idea runs through all five: the first move is to stop and stabilise, never to pull. Force turns a stuck needle into a broken one, and a bent needle into torn tissue. 五者一義：所先在止而安之，不在拔。強力者，使滯針成斷針，使彎針而裂肉。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Why does Lianquan CV23 carry a rule about retention specifically?","qZh":"廉泉 CV23 何以獨有留針之戒？","opts":[{"t":"Because swallowing moves the tissue around the needle and can break it","c":"吞嚥動之，可使針折","ok":1,"note":"CV23 廉泉 sits above the hyoid, needled obliquely toward the root of the tongue 0.5–0.8 cun. The patient will swallow — it is not something they can suspend — and swallowing moves the hyoid and the tongue base against a retained needle. So: do not retain, or retain only superficially. It is the point for post-stroke aphasia and difficulty swallowing, so the very patients who need it are the ones who swallow awkwardly. 廉泉在舌骨上緣，向舌根斜刺 0.5–0.8 寸。人必吞嚥，非其所能止；吞嚥則舌骨與舌根動於留針之側。故不可久留，或止於淺留。此穴主中風舌強失語與吞咽困難——最需之者，正吞嚥最不利者也。"},{"t":"Because the point bleeds easily","c":"其處易出血","ok":0,"note":"Bleeding is not the stated concern; movement and breakage are. 課件所言不在出血，而在動與折。"},{"t":"Because it is forbidden in pregnancy","c":"孕婦禁用","ok":0,"note":"That caution sits on the abdominal points, not on the throat. 此戒在腹部諸穴，不在咽喉。"},{"t":"Because deqi is unpleasant","c":"以其得氣不適","ok":0,"note":"Deqi at CV23 is local soreness and tightness at the root of the tongue — expected, and not the reason for the rule. 廉泉之得氣為舌根痠緊，其常也，非設戒之由。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"On the acupuncture paper, what does a Domain II safety question usually turn out to be asking?","qZh":"針灸卷之安全題（Domain II），其所實問者多為何？","opts":[{"t":"The angle, the depth, or the direction you must not take","c":"角度、深淺，或其所不可向","ok":1,"note":"Your own notes state it: <i>ACPL Domain II (15%) tests actual needling and its emergencies — angle and depth; Biomedicine tests universal precautions.</i> That single line tells you where to spend your study time. Hand hygiene, sharps and exposure protocol are real and important — and they are examined on the other paper. 課件明言：ACPL Domain II（15%）考實際針刺與其急症——角度與深淺；universal precautions 屬 Biomedicine。此一語，即告你力當用於何處。洗手、利器、暴露處置誠為要務——然其考在他卷。"},{"t":"Whether the point is allowed at all","c":"此穴可否用","ok":0,"note":"Only a handful are outright forbidden — CV8 神闕 chief among them. For nearly every other point the question is <i>how</i>, not <i>whether</i>. 絕對禁針者屈指可數，神闕為首。其餘幾皆問其「如何」，而非「可否」。"},{"t":"Which brand of needle to use","c":"用何廠之針","ok":0,"note":"Not examined, and not a clinical reasoning question. 非考點，亦非臨證之思。"},{"t":"How long to retain the needle in general","c":"留針之常時","ok":0,"note":"Retention is examined at specific points where it matters — CV22 and CV23, for instance — rather than as a general number. 留針之考，在其所係之穴，如天突、廉泉，而非泛論其時。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Your ACU-C-01 notes list findings that must not be explained by channel palpation alone. Which set is it?","qZh":"ACU-C-01 課件所列「不可僅憑經絡反應點判斷」者，為下列何組？","opts":[{"t":"Coughing blood, worsening cough, breathlessness, chest pain, cyanosis, high fever, unexplained weight loss, persistent hoarseness, irregular heartbeat, arm numbness or weakness","c":"咯血、咳嗽加重、呼吸困難、胸痛、發紺、高熱、體重不明下降、持續聲嘶、心律不整、上肢麻木無力","ok":1,"note":"Your notes put this in writing on the Lung channel page: tenderness, nodules or texture changes along a channel cannot diagnose pneumonia, airway disease, thyroid disease, arrhythmia or malignancy. Channel palpation is a pattern-differentiation aid; these findings need history, examination, imaging and specialist assessment. Recognising when to hand a patient on is itself part of the safety domain. 課件於肺經頁明書之：經絡上之壓痛、結節、皮膚彈性或觸感，不能診斷肺炎、氣管病變、甲狀腺疾病、心律不整或惡性腫瘤。經絡觸診者，辨證之助耳；此類見症當憑病史、理學檢查、影像與專科評估。知何時當轉介，本即安全之一事。"},{"t":"Dry mouth, poor appetite, mild fatigue","c":"口乾、納差、微倦","ok":0,"note":"Ordinary pattern findings, reasoned about normally. 尋常之證，如常辨之可也。"},{"t":"Tenderness at LU6, a nodule at LU5","c":"孔最壓痛、尺澤結節","ok":0,"note":"Those are the palpation findings themselves — the point of the note is what they may <i>not</i> be used to conclude. 此即所觸之見；課件所言者，乃其所<b>不可</b>據以斷者。"},{"t":"A wiry pulse and a red tongue","c":"脈弦舌紅","ok":0,"note":"Standard diagnostic signs within the system. 此本系統內之常診。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which statement about this deck is correct?","qZh":"關於本組，下列何者為是？","opts":[{"t":"It drills the acupuncture safety domain — angle, depth, forbidden points, accidents — and leaves universal precautions to the Biomedicine paper","c":"本組所練者針灸之安全域：角度、深淺、禁針穴、意外；universal precautions 歸 Biomedicine 卷","ok":1,"note":"That division is your own note's, not an invention here. It also means: when this deck and your course differ, your course is right, and telling me so is how the deck gets better. 此分即出你自己的筆記，非此處所立。且其義為：本組與課程有異者，以課程為是；告我，則本組益善。"},{"t":"It replaces your clinical training and your supervisor","c":"可代臨床訓練與指導老師","ok":0,"note":"Nothing in a game could. 凡遊戲所為，皆不足以此。"},{"t":"Safety questions are a small part of the acupuncture paper","c":"安全題於針灸卷所佔甚微","ok":0,"note":"Domain II is 15% — the same weight as point location and as needling technique. 安全域佔 15%，與定位、針法同重。"},{"t":"These cautions are the same on every channel","c":"諸經之戒皆同","ok":0,"note":"They are point-specific, which is why they are learned point by point. 其戒繫於穴，故當逐穴而記。"}]}]};
